==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Orbital Platform Armageddon''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Orbital Annihilator Ragnarok''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Mighty Rekon Korps is a great powerhouse versus traited enemies; able to deal a whopping 10,486 DPS at level 30, Rekon Korps will easily burn nearly any traited enemy to ashes. Mighty Rekon Korps also has Zombie Killer, becoming an extremely useful aide to deal with most Zombies. However, it's better to either send them after Zombies unburrow, or to interrupt Zombies from burrowing (this can be done if you knock the Zombies back just when they attempt to burrow) so they don't simply burrow past Rekon. The [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] can accomplish this.

Mighty Rekon Korps can be seen as a cheaper and heavier-hitting, but frailer [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Gao]] that won't do a thing against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] or [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies. If there is Traitless or Metal support along with a traited threat, bring units such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] to support it. Like most other Uber Rares, Rekon Korps also requires tanks and meatshields along with it, as they're quite frail. On the other hand, they have 8 knockbacks, which improves their survivability. Try to prevent bulky Zombie Enemies from burrowing to your backline, as they can interrupt the flow of meatshields, and leave Rekon unprotected.

Since they don't attack Traitless enemies, in stages where the initial peons are Doge, Snache, Those Guys, or other traitless peons, they can be efficiently stacked by the base. Be sure to use [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] if the peons are buffed. Due to the long attack animation, they may get interrupted or miss enemies that get knocked back easily (such as [[Gory]] variants). Furthermore, sniper enemies like [[Hackey]] and [[Tackey]] will constantly knockback Rekon, so do not use him on stages with them.

This unit works well against [[Winged Pigge]], as they have great range and damage. Also, even if reached, they can be knocked back easily, and their long attack animation will let the weaken effect expire just before they attack, making Winged Pigge's weaken ability basically ineffective against this unit.

Beside Traitless, Mighty Rekon Corps also can't attack [[:Category:EVA Angel Enemies|EVA Angels]] or [[:Category:Witch Enemies|Witches]].

==='''True Form'''===
Orbital Annihilator Ragnarok gains more range, attack power and the [[Omni Strike]] ability. These all increases Ragnarok's general usage, with the Omni Strike additionally increasing their usage against Zombies, letting Ragnarok sometimes intercept those who burrow past him, though not too far. However, this Omni Strike doesn't add any forward piercing range to Ragnarok's attacks, as the standing range is the same as the maximum effective range.

Just like before, Ragnarok won't do anything against Traitless, Metal or collab-exclusive types, which can be exploited for stacking.

==='''Talents'''===
The first talent of note is the ability to survive an otherwise lethal hit, which is particularly useful For Ragnarok. Their range usually serves them well even after activating this talent, though some enemies can push past this range advantage, and Zombies in particular can burrow to defeat them outright. Regardless, the ability to safely reposition once more can be useful.

The second talent of note is Curse Immunity. This is largely useful due to how the Target Only ability works, since any unit with this ability can no longer attack when cursed. With this talent, [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies can no longer turn Ragnarok into a sitting duck with a single Curse, and Ragnarok can finally strike back with their great destructive power.

The third talent reduces recharge time, which is however underwhelming in this case. Without this talent, their recharge time is almost three full minutes, so any means to speed it up is welcome. However, even with this talent maxed out, their recharge time is around 2 and a half minutes, which is still ridiculously long. It can definitely be an improvement, especially in longer battles, but it does not do enough to be worth the NP cost most of the time.

Finally, like most Cats, they have Attack Buff and HP Buff talents. As a stat-based unit, Ragnarok benefits from both of these, especially Attack Buff. These talents are worthwhile mainly for those who have lots of NP already. Otherwise, [[Catseye]]s will do good anyways.

