==Trivia==
*Orbital Platform Armageddon appear to be a foil to [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Guardians]].
**Both units attack via surprise ambush: Armageddon engages enemies from outer space through a portal, while the Subterra Guardians surface from deep within the Earth's crust.
**The mustachioed cat works as the "bait" for Armageddon's operations and summons them at will with a big red button, whereas the eyepatch cat appears to unknowingly send signals to the Subterra Guardians through a metal detector.
**The mustachioed cat appears calm and collected throughout Armageddon's attack animation, while the eyepatch cat loses composure and panics.
*This unit's name is misspelled as "Mighty Recon Korps" on the IRON LEGION banner.
*Mighty Rekon Korps' description in the IRON LEGION event info incorrectly states that it "survives when killed by a Zombie". This is most likely a mistranslation.
*There is a spelling error in the Evolved Form's description in [[The Battle Cats Unite!]] where "strikes" is misspelled as "stikes".
*The Mighty Rekon Korps have the highest knockback count among all [[:Category:Focused Target Cats|Focused Target Cats]].
*Because Mighty Rekon Korps cannot target traitless enemies, it is possible to max out the cat limit with only Orbital Platform Armageddon or Orbital Annihilator Ragnarok in most stages with traitless enemies. Doing so will create a glitchy mess of sprites if they were to all attack. This is caused from the high amount of sprites and the size of his sprites used on his sprite sheet.
*Its normal form, evolved form and true form says it has [[Massive Damage|Massive Damage]], but refers to the damage it does and not the ability.
*Orbital Platform Armageddon's Cat Combo, Independence Day, is a reference to [[Wikipedia:Independence Day (1996)|Independence Day]] by Roland Emmerich.
*In early versions of the game, when Orbital Platform Armageddons or Orbital Annihilator Ragnaroks are stacked without attacking, it would cause a [https://www.youtube.com/shorts/o65Ynuyj7rg glitch] that caused other sprites to appear in the attack animation.

